      "content": "You're a high-risk patient, so it's best to be cautious. I'm not saying you need to rush to the ER, but I do recommend you take a few extra precautions. Take an ibuprofen or acetaminophen to help with the headache, and apply an ice pack to the bump to reduce swelling. As for Eliquis, you can continue taking it as usual, but make sure to monitor your INR levels closely - if it's a bit off, you might want to adjust your dosage.",
